WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
Whey Material.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:07.010
A third-party lab test of a whey tank, before and after White Leaf blue light.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.250
Whey is rich in nutrients, and that makes a stored whey tank a breeding ground for bacteria.

00:00:14.203 --> 00:00:19.610
On September 1, 2026, a sample from the tank went to Clean Water Testing,

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.430
a state-certified lab in Appleton, Wisconsin.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:28.970
Coliform bacteria were present, at more than 2,419.8 MPN.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:30.770
A heavy load.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.770
White Leaf then hung one oval, 240-watt, all-blue fixture inside the tank.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.450
It floods the whey with continuous violet-blue light,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.130
in a selected band of the visible spectrum.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.069
The light shines straight down onto the whey, every hour of every day.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.030
On November 2, 2026, with the blue light running, a new sample went to the same lab.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.430
Coliform: none detected.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.770
E. coli was not detected in either test.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:06.990
Before the light: more than 2,419.8 MPN.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.430
After the light: none detected.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.730
The light runs 24 hours a day.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:18.349
At night, the white tank glows violet-blue, as the light keeps working on the whey.

00:01:19.281 --> 00:01:20.330
One tank.

00:01:20.861 --> 00:01:22.950
Two independent lab tests.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.330
A heavy coliform load before, and none detected after.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.230
White Leaf Technology Group.

